{
  "comment": "One list for the whole UI tour (scripts/ui-tour.sh): web = path on the dev web, app = route the iOS/iPad/Mac app opens (TourDriver.swift). {project} and {form} are replaced by projectId / formId (or TOUR_PROJECT_ID / TOUR_FORM_ID). Legal (14 Oct 2026): {legalDoc} = the newest [TEST] document (GET /api/legal/documents?q=[TEST], or TOUR_LEGAL_DOC_ID), {legalForm} = the general request link path /f/legal-<token> (GET /api/legal/request-links, or TOUR_LEGAL_FORM_PATH), {webBase} = the dev web origin; looked up at run time, and a screen whose value is not found is recorded as 'skipped: <reason>'. appTab = the Legal tab the app tour taps after landing; appOpen legalDoc = it taps that document's row. account nonmember = shot signed in as TOUR_NONMEMBER_EMAIL (qa6, not invited to Legal), web only, skipped without TOUR_NONMEMBER_PASSWORD. Order = order in index.html. pages = the app tour's page cap for that screen when above TOUR_MAX_PAGES; sideways = how many half-view sideways shots a board or table gets (default 1). Dashboards (14 Oct 2026): {outlet} / {socmed} = the QA Outlet Sales / Social Media Report project, found at run time over the API (GET /api/projects: the project named 'ZZ QA Manager Outlet' / 'ZZ QA Social Media Report', else the first 'ZZ QA' project of type OUTLET_SALES / SOCIAL_MEDIA_REPORT; TOUR_OUTLET_PROJECT_ID / TOUR_SOCMED_PROJECT_ID override), {outletDay} = a day other than today (the calendar already shows today's panel): the newest night waiting for its report, else reported, else with its own daily target, {socmedDay} = the newest date up to today with figures, this month or the one before. webVariants = the web variants that shoot the screen (default all; the collapsed sidebar is desktop only, a phone has no rail). webAfterTaps = buttons the web tour presses after the shots, to leave the page as it found it (Expand sidebar). webTaps / appTaps = buttons the web / app tour presses in order after landing, 'A|B' = the English or Indonesian label, a leading '?' = only when the next one is not on screen yet (the iPhone's + menu), then a '~' = the label holds it (a leaderboard row: 'QA Dev' in '7, QA Dev, Level 6 …'). profile (app only, run 18): the person a leaderboard row opens.",
